1
00:00:00,550 --> 00:00:06,920
Today I'll show you how to turn a hand sketch of a floor plan and a few photos into a furnished 3D flat, with SOMA AI.

2
00:00:07,870 --> 00:00:11,523
And then we try out ideas, like a round table in the kitchen.

3
00:00:11,523 --> 00:00:12,960
No CAD knowledge needed.

4
00:00:14,950 --> 00:00:15,721
We use SOMA.

5
00:00:15,721 --> 00:00:19,960
It's free and open source, and you can download it at somacad.app.

6
00:00:20,910 --> 00:00:22,275
SOMA itself is free.

7
00:00:22,275 --> 00:00:24,663
For SOMA AI, you bring your own AI:

8
00:00:24,663 --> 00:00:27,188
a ChatGPT subscription or an API key.

9
00:00:29,550 --> 00:00:32,550
I start with a new model, Flat, and import my material:

10
00:00:32,550 --> 00:00:35,713
a sketch of the floor plan, and a few photos of each room.

11
00:00:35,713 --> 00:00:37,840
SOMA copies them into the model folder.

12
00:00:40,983 --> 00:00:42,056
The sketch is simple:

13
00:00:42,056 --> 00:00:44,970
the rooms, the doors and windows, and a few measurements.

14
00:00:44,970 --> 00:00:47,985
Just like you would draw your own flat with a tape measure.

15
00:00:51,717 --> 00:00:55,994
The photos show a historic flat in Heidelberg that is now a small museum.

16
00:00:55,994 --> 00:00:57,927
We drew the sketch to match them.

17
00:01:03,683 --> 00:01:05,433
Everything is ready.

18
00:01:05,433 --> 00:01:08,494
Now we build the flat with SOMA AI.

19
00:01:08,494 --> 00:01:11,643
I click its tab, and pick the model:

20
00:01:11,643 --> 00:01:12,693
GPT-6.1 Sol.

21
00:01:16,550 --> 00:01:23,507
I add the sketch as a picture, and ask for the floor, the walls, the door openings and the windows, as drawn.

22
00:01:23,507 --> 00:01:24,209
No ceiling.

23
00:01:24,209 --> 00:01:27,400
And it should ask me first if anything is unclear.

24
00:01:32,983 --> 00:01:35,401
Before it starts, it asks two questions:

25
00:01:35,401 --> 00:01:41,384
keep the overall size of eight by seven meters, and use window widths it estimated from the sketch.

26
00:01:41,384 --> 00:01:43,016
I take its recommendations.

27
00:01:43,966 --> 00:01:45,094
Then it gets to work:

28
00:01:45,094 --> 00:01:50,896
it lays out the walls as drawn, builds the flat, and looks at a picture of the result to check its own work.

29
00:01:51,846 --> 00:01:52,878
Here's the flat:

30
00:01:52,878 --> 00:02:00,040
eight by seven meters inside, walls 2.6 meters high, six door openings, and four windows with frames and glass.

31
00:02:00,040 --> 00:02:01,976
No ceiling, so we can look in.

32
00:02:04,733 --> 00:02:06,634
Every room sits where the sketch has it:

33
00:02:06,634 --> 00:02:10,863
the bedroom and the bath at the back, the living room and the kitchen on the street side.

34
00:02:15,133 --> 00:02:16,235
Now the furniture.

35
00:02:16,235 --> 00:02:23,823
I add the photos of all the rooms to the chat, and ask SOMA AI to model the furniture it sees, each piece in the right room.

36
00:02:31,066 --> 00:02:35,982
It looks at every photo, works out which room it shows, and builds each piece from simple shapes.

37
00:02:35,982 --> 00:02:40,796
Then it checks the layout in a picture, and moves the wardrobe a little where it was too tight.

38
00:02:41,746 --> 00:02:43,248
And there it is, furnished.

39
00:02:43,248 --> 00:02:47,476
Every piece is a part of its own, and the structure tree sorts them by room.

40
00:02:50,280 --> 00:02:53,185
To see it like a floor plan, I use the viewing tools.

41
00:02:53,185 --> 00:02:55,432
They only change the view, not the model:

42
00:02:55,432 --> 00:02:59,597
the view from the top, and a section that cuts the walls at about one meter.

43
00:03:02,780 --> 00:03:04,527
Now you see every room at once:

44
00:03:04,527 --> 00:03:12,757
the red sofa and the sewing table in the living room, the beds and the cot in the bedroom, the old kitchen range and the dresser, and the bathtub.

45
00:03:14,913 --> 00:03:15,963
Now the fun part:

46
00:03:15,963 --> 00:03:17,014
trying out ideas.

47
00:03:17,014 --> 00:03:20,288
How would the kitchen look with a round dining table?

48
00:03:20,288 --> 00:03:22,883
I click the table, and send it to SOMA AI.

49
00:03:26,280 --> 00:03:27,732
Then I say what I want:

50
00:03:27,732 --> 00:03:33,353
a round table, one meter across, with four chairs around it, and the diameter adjustable.

51
00:03:35,980 --> 00:03:42,487
SOMA AI swaps the table for a round one, puts four chairs around it, and checks that even the largest size still fits.

52
00:03:42,487 --> 00:03:45,630
For that, it moves the set a little away from the window.

53
00:03:46,580 --> 00:03:50,654
Here's the kitchen with a round table, one meter across, and four chairs facing it.

54
00:03:50,654 --> 00:03:52,470
The rest of the flat stays as it was.

55
00:03:55,313 --> 00:03:59,645
The diameter is now a parameter, from 80 centimeters to 1.2 meters.

56
00:03:59,645 --> 00:04:04,883
Drag the slider, and SOMA rebuilds the flat by itself, and the chairs move along.

57
00:04:09,880 --> 00:04:12,880
Every step of SOMA AI is saved in the history at the bottom.

58
00:04:12,880 --> 00:04:15,930
So you can try as many ideas as you like, and always go back.

59
00:04:17,580 --> 00:04:18,174
That's it:

60
00:04:18,174 --> 00:04:22,868
from a hand sketch and a few photos to a furnished flat in 3D, without any CAD.

61
00:04:22,868 --> 00:04:26,670
Get SOMA for free at somacad.app, and try it with your own flat.
